<p class="lt-chem-370953">Figure 4.1: Transfer of spin density by the spin polarization mechanism. According to the Pauli principle, the two electrons in the C-H bond orbital must have opposite spin state. If the unpaired electron resides in a  orbital on the  atom, for other electrons on the same  atom the same spin state is slightly favored, as this minimizes electrostatic repulsion. Hence, for the electron at the  atom, the opposite spin state (left panel) is slightly favored over the same spin state (right panel). Positive spin density in the  orbital on the  atom induces some negative spin density in the  orbital on the  atom.</p>



