<p class="lt-chem-370953">In Eq. (4.7), the term  is secular and must always be kept. Usually, the high-field approximation does hold for the electron spin, so that all terms containing  or  operators are non-secular and can be dropped. The truncated hyperfine Hamiltonian thus reads</p>

