<p class="lt-chem-370953">Figure 10.7: Characterization of oxygen accessibility at spin-labeled site V229C in major plant light harvesting complex LHCII by CW progressive power saturation. (a) Ribbon model of LHCII with green with its carotenoid cofactors (yellow, violet) and space-filling model of residue 229 (red, marked by an arrow). The pink planes correspond to the lipid headgroup layer of the thylakoid membrane in chloroplasts. (b) Progressive power saturation curves in the absence (blue) and presence (red) of oxygen.</p>



